# orchard-row.xyz rotated 90 deg about Z, translated (2, -1.5, 0).
# GROUND TRUTH mis-alignment for the Auto-Register E2E test.
#
# 90 deg is load-bearing: plain ICP recovers 25-60 deg on this data by
# itself, so a smaller angle lets the ICP refinement stage mask a totally
# broken coarse stage (verified by sabotaging it and watching the test still
# pass). At 90 deg plain ICP fails hard while the coarse stage recovers the
# pose exactly, so the test can only pass if global registration works.
